  "evidence": "P1 (533-545) shows a sustained offset in N/E/U with return by ~545; interior points (e.g., 538–544) remain displaced consistently, supporting a genuine temporary platform. P2 (540) is an isolated point coinciding with P1’s interior and P3’s onset—no sustained shift or return, likely noise or step artifact. P3 (540-587) overlaps P1 and includes the large spike at 540 (matching P2/P3 onset_offsets), but no opposing return across axes; instead, observations continue drifting downward (e.g., N from ~-4 to -9 between 540–587), inconsistent with temporary offset. P4 (575-587) is fully embedded in P3’s interval and lacks independent return; its small offset is likely residual motion, not a separate platform. P5 (588) is a single-point jump with no return and coincides with a nuisance step (per numerical_tool_evidence), indicating permanent step, not temporary. Only P1 satisfies criteria: sustained shift + opposing return across axes, interior consistency, and physical plausibility.",
  "pair_ids": ["P1"]
}
